Hi Avery,

Here's what's new on GitHub this month for organizations on Team.

Copilot code review, generally available
Copilot now reviews every pull request automatically, flagging likely bugs, missing tests, and security issues before a human reviewer looks. Enable it per repository under Settings > Rules.

Merge queue for every plan
Keep your default branch green by letting GitHub batch and test PRs before they land.

Actions cost insights
A new usage page breaks down minutes by workflow, repository, and runner type, so you can see which CI jobs are eating the budget.

Also: Dependabot groups related updates into one PR, and the new issue types (bug, task, epic) roll up into project views.

See the changelog: https://explore.github.com/l/changelog-0903

Happy shipping,
